camera: advertise the front camera, and fix SENSOR_ORIENTATION

Two ROM metadata bugs, both device-visible and both breaking real apps.

1) The device tree copied android.hardware.camera.xml, which declares
   android.hardware.camera - a BACK camera. These devices have a single front
   camera and none was advertised at all. CameraX's CameraValidator only looks
   for a back camera when FEATURE_CAMERA is advertised, so the bogus feature
   failed validation device-wide ("Camera LensFacing verification failed") and
   CameraX retried init forever, hanging any app that did not set an
   availableCamerasLimiter. Copy android.hardware.camera.front.xml instead,
   which declares camera.any + camera.front.

2) The sensor is landscape-mounted, matching the landscape-natural 960x480
   panel, and the driver flips it 180 degrees so frames arrive upright - but
   the MediaTek HAL reports a phone-style 270, so every client that correctly
   rotates by SENSOR_ORIENTATION produced a sideways image. The value comes
   from DevMetaInfo::queryDeviceWantedOrientation() inside libcam.utils.so and
   cannot be corrected in the blobs, so camera.device@1.0-impl now honours
   ro.camera.sensor_orientation, where both HAL1 clients and the camera2
   legacy shim pick it up.

Verified on device: features correct, CameraX initialises with zero validator
failures, dumpsys reports Orientation: 0, and captures come out upright.

diff --git a/mt8163.mk b/mt8163.mk
index 5259e13..1ab42c4 100644
--- a/device/amazon/mt8163-common/mt8163.mk
+++ b/device/amazon/mt8163-common/mt8163.mk
@@ -54,12 +54,21 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 
 # Camera
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    android.hardware.camera.provider@2.4-impl \
     camera.device@1.0-impl \
     camera.device@3.2-impl \
+    libcamera_shim \
     libsensorndkbridge
 
+# These devices have a single front-facing camera and no back camera, so
+# advertise camera.front rather than the plain camera.xml (which declares
+# android.hardware.camera, i.e. a back camera). Getting this wrong is not
+# cosmetic: CameraX's CameraValidator only checks for a back camera when
+# FEATURE_CAMERA is advertised, so the bogus feature made it fail device-wide
+# with "Camera LensFacing verification failed" and retry init forever in any
+# app that does not set an availableCamerasLimiter.
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-    frameworks/native/data/etc/android.hardware.camera.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR)/etc/permissions/android.hardware.camera.xml
+    frameworks/native/data/etc/android.hardware.camera.front.xml:$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR)/etc/permissions/android.hardware.camera.front.xml
 
 # Display
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index b50db70..aedd1e9 100644
--- a/device/amazon/cronos/device.mk
+++ b/device/amazon/cronos/device.mk
@@ -97,6 +97,16 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
     $(call find-copy-subdir-files,*,$(LOCAL_PATH)/configs/wifi/,$(TARGET_COPY_OUT_VENDOR)/etc/wifi)
 
+# Camera
+# The OV02B10 is landscape-mounted, matching this device's landscape-natural
+# 960x480 panel, and the sensor driver flips it 180 degrees so frames arrive
+# upright. The MediaTek HAL nonetheless reports a phone-style 270, which makes
+# every client that correctly rotates by SENSOR_ORIENTATION come out sideways.
+# The value comes from inside libcam.utils.so and cannot be fixed in the blob,
+# so camera.device@1.0-impl honours this override instead.
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
+    ro.camera.sensor_orientation=0
+
 # Inherit from mt8163-common
 $(call inherit-product, device/amazon/mt8163-common/mt8163.mk)
 
(The camera.device@1.0-impl side lives in patches/0005-*, which touches the
same file.)
